{
  "dom_id": "step-e22729",
  "name": "Example: Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions and Mixed Numbers",
  "problem": "A submarine descends $1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\,\\text{m}$ each minute from sea level. What is the submarine's elevation after $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes?",
  "worked_solution": "The submarine descends $1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\,\\text{m}$ each minute.\n\nSince the elevation decreases, the change each minute is $-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}.$\n\nThe descent lasts $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes, so the total change in elevation is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8} = -\\dfrac{1\\times8 + 3}{8} = -\\dfrac{11}{8}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{8}\\right)\n= -\\dfrac{8 \\times 11}{3 \\times 8}\n= -\\dfrac{11}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the submarine's elevation after $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes is $-\\dfrac{11}{3}\\,\\text{m}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
